\section*{Overview}
This document provides a high-level overview of the Suprakernel Sovereign
Architecture, a self-building autonomous intelligence system integrating
real-time manifold dynamics, Lyapunov stability enforcement, and adaptive
kernel mutation. The architecture is designed for deployment on large-scale
GPU clusters and supports continuous self-modification under strict
mathematical safety guarantees.

\section{System Objectives}
The suprakernel architecture is engineered to:
\begin{itemize}
    \item ingest high-bandwidth telemetry streams through zero-copy ring buffers,
    \item project state vectors onto a Riemannian stress manifold,
    \item autonomously mutate CUDA/PTX kernels via JIT compilation,
    \item enforce Lyapunov negativity and Control Barrier Function (CBF) invariance,
    \item maintain global asymptotic stability under extreme stress conditions.
\end{itemize}

\section{Core Components}
\subsection{Sensor Ingestion Gate}
The ingestion subsystem processes FITS/HDFS streams, cluster telemetry, and
state vectors $p(t)$ using lock-free ring buffers to ensure bounded latency and
memory integrity.

\subsection{Riemannian Stress Manifold}
State vectors are mapped to the stress manifold $\mathcal{M}_{\text{stress}}$
via the $\Omega$-mapping operator. The Jacobian determinant $J(p)$ is monitored
continuously to prevent topological inversion.

\subsection{Autonomous Kernel Mutation Loop}
The four-stage autodidact cycle:
\[
\text{Observe} \rightarrow \text{Orient} \rightarrow \text{Mutate} \rightarrow \text{Verify},
\]
governs runtime kernel evolution. Mutation proposals $\Delta K$ are constrained
by Lyapunov and CBF inequalities to ensure safe self-modification.

\subsection{Lyapunov Stability Enforcement}
The candidate Lyapunov function:
\begin{equation}
L(p) = \frac{1}{2}\|p - p^*\|^2 + U(p) +
\frac{1}{2}\gamma(t)\max(0,-J(p))^2,
\end{equation}
is used to certify global asymptotic stability. All valid trajectories satisfy:
\begin{equation}
\dot{L}(p) < 0.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Control Barrier Function (CBF) Safety Layer}
The safe region:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C} = \{ p \mid h(p) \ge 0 \},
\end{equation}
is enforced through real-time quadratic programs ensuring:
\begin{equation}
\dot{h}(p) + \gamma_{\text{CBF}} h(p) \ge 0.
\end{equation}

